---
layout: v3.njk
---
{#- Security incident tracker. Data: src/_data/incidents.yml; computed fields: incidents.11tydata.js -#}
<main id="main" class="container inc">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</li><li aria-current="page">Incident tracker</li></ol></nav>

  <header class="inc-hero">
    <p class="inc-hero__kicker"><span class="inc-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Vendor risk · checked <time datetime="{{ incidents.checked | iso }}">{{ incidents.checked | displayDate }}</time></p>
    <h1 class="h-display">Security incidents at KYC and identity verification vendors</h1>
    <p class="inc-hero__lede">Identity vendors hold passport scans, selfies and screening files for thousands of companies. This tracker lists every breach, data exposure and security incident we could confirm at the vendors we review, with what was exposed, what the vendor said and where the facts come from.</p>
    <dl class="inc-stats">
      <div><dt>Incidents tracked</dt><dd class="num">{{ stats.total }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Vendors involved</dt><dd class="num">{{ stats.vendors }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Involved ID documents or ID numbers</dt><dd class="num">{{ stats.idDocs }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>In the last 24 months</dt><dd class="num">{{ stats.recent }}</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </header>

  <div class="inc-layout">
    <aside class="inc-side" aria-label="About this tracker">
      <div class="inc-side__box">
        <h2>How to read it</h2>
        <ul class="inc-legend">
          <li><span class="inc-sev inc-sev--high" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><b>High</b> ID documents, biometrics or national ID numbers</span></li>
          <li><span class="inc-sev inc-sev--medium" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><b>Medium</b> contact or account data</span></li>
          <li><span class="inc-sev inc-sev--low" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><b>Low</b> no personal data reported</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Claims made in lawsuits are allegations, not findings. The vendor's response sits next to every entry.</p>
      </div>
      <nav class="inc-side__box" aria-label="Jump to a vendor">
        <h2>Vendors</h2>
        {%- for x in list %}<a class="inc-jump" href="#{{ x.id }}"><span>{{ x.vendor }}</span><span class="num">{{ x.date | displayDate }}</span></a>{% endfor %}
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <div class="inc-feed">
      {%- for y in years %}
      <section class="inc-year" aria-labelledby="y-{{ y }}">
        <h2 id="y-{{ y }}" class="inc-year__label num">{{ y }}</h2>
        <ol class="inc-list">
          {%- for x in list %}{% if x.year == y %}
          <li class="inc-item inc-item--{{ x.sensitivity }}" id="{{ x.id }}">
            <article class="inc-card" aria-labelledby="{{ x.id }}-h">
              <div class="inc-card__top">
                <div class="inc-card__vendor">
                  {%- if x.p and x.p.logo and x.p.logo.src %}<span class="inc-logo"><img src="{{ x.p.logo.wordmark or x.p.logo.src }}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>{% endif %}
                  <div>
                    {%- if x.p %}<a class="inc-card__name" href="/providers/{{ x.slug }}/">{{ x.vendor }}</a>{% else %}<span class="inc-card__name">{{ x.vendor }}</span>{% endif %}
                    <span class="inc-card__date"><time datetime="{{ x.date | iso }}">{{ x.date | displayDate }}</time> · {{ x.occurred }}</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="inc-tags">
                  <span class="pill">{{ x.typeLabel }}</span>
                  <span class="pill inc-status inc-status--{{ x.status }}">{{ x.statusLabel }}</span>
                  {%- if x.counted == false %}<span class="pill pill--soon">Not counted in score</span>{% endif %}
                </div>
              </div>
              <h3 id="{{ x.id }}-h" class="inc-card__title">{{ x.title }}</h3>
              <p class="inc-card__summary">{{ x.summary }}</p>
              <dl class="inc-facts">
                <div><dt>Sensitivity</dt><dd><span class="inc-sev inc-sev--{{ x.sensitivity }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ x.sensLabel }}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Scale</dt><dd>{{ x.scale }}</dd></div>
                <div class="inc-facts--wide"><dt>Data involved</dt><dd class="inc-chips">{% for t in x.data %}<span class="chip">{{ t }}</span>{% endfor %}</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <div class="inc-response">
                <h4>What {{ x.vendor }} says</h4>
                <p>{{ x.response }}</p>
              </div>
              <p class="inc-since"><b>Since:</b> {{ x.since }}</p>
              <div class="inc-card__foot">
                <ol class="inc-sources">{% for s in x.sources %}<li><a href="{{ s.url }}" rel="nofollow noopener">{{ s.title }}</a> <span>{{ s.publisher }}</span></li>{% endfor %}</ol>
                <div class="inc-links">{% if x.news %}<a class="pill-link" href="{{ x.news }}">Read our report</a>{% endif %}{% if x.p %}<a class="pill-link" href="/providers/{{ x.slug }}/">{{ x.vendor }} review</a>{% endif %}</div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </li>
          {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
        </ol>
      </section>
      {%- endfor %}

      <section class="inc-table" aria-labelledby="tbl-h">
        <h2 id="tbl-h" class="h-section">All incidents at a glance</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <caption>Security incidents at reviewed KYC, IDV and AML vendors, newest first, as of {{ incidents.checked | displayDate }}</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Date</th><th scope="col">Vendor</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Sensitivity</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">In score</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {%- for x in list %}
              <tr><td class="num"><a href="#{{ x.id }}">{{ x.date | displayDate }}</a></td><th scope="row">{{ x.vendor }}</th><td>{{ x.typeLabel }}</td><td>{{ x.sensitivity | capitalize }}</td><td>{{ x.statusLabel }}</td><td>{% if x.counted == false %}No{% else %}Yes{% endif %}</td></tr>
              {%- endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="inc-rules" aria-labelledby="rules-h">
        <h2 id="rules-h" class="h-section">What goes in, and what does not</h2>
        <div class="grid-3">
          <div class="card card--pad"><h3 class="card__title">Included</h3><p>Data breaches, exposures of personal data, confirmed security incidents and regulatory actions at vendors we review, reported since 2024.</p></div>
          <div class="card card--pad"><h3 class="card__title">Not included</h3><p>Private lawsuits with no breach behind them, such as biometric consent suits, and incidents at a vendor's customer that did not touch the vendor's systems.</p></div>
          <div class="card card--pad"><h3 class="card__title">Sources</h3><p>The vendor's own statement, official breach notices, regulators and courts first. News reports are used to add detail, and are named.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="inc-note">Every vendor is treated the same way, including those we earn money from. Vendors can send a response or a correction to <a href="mailto:support@beverified.org?subject=Incident%20tracker">support@beverified.org</a>, and we add it to the entry when a source supports it. Incidents feed the track record part of a provider's score, as described in <a href="/methodology/">our methodology</a>; entries marked "Not counted in score" do not.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
